# standard.process — EAV-native process-control binding (§27 planned namespace).
#
# Parity with semsc's `std/process` surface, the EAV-clean way: process control
# is a capability-mediated effect (§8/§11), never ambient. `exitProcess` and
# `abortProcess` are `body runtimeBinding` ops over the libc `exit`/`abort` ABI
# symbols (resolved in-process by the JIT); the compiler carries no process
# knowledge (README ss11/ss26). A caller that activates either inherits the
# `terminate process.self` effect and must cover it with a capability.

standardProcess is module
standardProcess path standard.process
standardProcess purpose "Capability-gated process termination over the libc exit/abort ABI"
standardProcess invariant "Termination is a capability-mediated effect, not ambient authority"

processTerminator is capability
processTerminator grants terminate process.self
processTerminator purpose "Authority to terminate the current process"

exitProcess is operation
exitProcess in code Int32
exitProcess effect terminate process.self
exitProcess uses processTerminator
exitProcess body runtimeBinding exit
exitProcess purpose "Terminate the process with the given exit code (libc exit)"

abortProcess is operation
abortProcess effect terminate process.self
abortProcess uses processTerminator
abortProcess body runtimeBinding abort
abortProcess purpose "Abort the process immediately (libc abort)"
